"""You can see the description of the task using the code specified in the title on leetcode.
This program has O(n) complexity by time and O(n) by space.

After reading the problem, I realized I could solve it, but at a high cost. 
It feels like there’s an elegant solution out there - a thought that constantly distracts me from actually writing *any* solution at all.

We are interested in the sum and the count of "?" marks.
Alice always aims to increase the larger side, while Bob tries to decrease it. 
Once there is no more room left, the opponent simply tries to slow down the growth of the opposing side. 
If the sides end up equal, Alice loses.
It is also worth adding that if Alice makes the last move, she has definitely won.

BUT TURNING THIS INTO ELEGANT CODE took me over an hour.
"""

class Solution:
    def sumGame(self, num: str) -> bool:
        half = len(num) // 2
        left, right = num[:half], num[half:]
        sum_dif = (sum(int(d) for d in left if d != '?') - sum(int(d) for d in right if d != '?'))
        q_dif = left.count('?') - right.count('?')
        if q_dif % 2:
            return True
        return sum_dif != -9 * (q_dif // 2)
